  "summary_en": "SDAIA's May 2025 document introduces the National AI Index, a measurement framework assessing Saudi government entities' readiness to adopt AI. It sets three pillars, seven sub-pillars, 23 domains, six maturity levels, a questionnaire-based assessment process, and reporting. It contains no robotics or embodied-AI content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Index has three pillars (Directions, Enablers, Outputs), seven sub-pillars and 23 domains",
   "Six maturity levels from Level 0 (absence) to Level 5 (Pioneer) based on percentage scores",
   "Measurement via workshops, questionnaires with evidence, and expert verification",
   "Entities should implement SDAIA frameworks such as Generative AI and Deepfake Guidelines",
   "SDAIA issues national and per-entity reports with recommendations; annual review of the index"
